# Per-record inclusion diagnostic: carries person-level FRS survey weights
# and earnings for individually ranked records, so it is a licensed-microdata
# derivative and must never be committed. Regenerate with
# `make assignment-inclusion`.
/results/assignment_inclusion_diagnostic.json

# Compiled manuscript: `paper/main.pdf` is deliberately tracked as a
# convenience artifact, accepting the stale-PDF hazard the earlier rule here
# warned about. Mitigation: rebuild the PDF in the same commit as any source
# change (CI does not compile the paper). LaTeX build residue stays ignored.
paper/*.log
paper/*.aux
paper/*.out
paper/*.fls
paper/*.fdb_latexmk

# LFS/FRS benchmark microdata: both carry person-level FRS records
# (person_id, age, gender, employment_income, survey weight) and are licensed
# under the UKDS end-user licence, so they must never be committed. The
# manuscript reads results/lfs_qrf_benchmark_summary.json, an aggregate
# derived from them. Rebuild both with
# `make lfs-benchmarks LFS_TAB=/path/to/panel.tab`.
/results/lfs_imputed_frs_transition_parameters.csv.gz
/results/lfs_qrf_benchmark.csv.gz
